# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command rom
shell rust
usage 1   rom hash [-r] [--comparable] <path>...
usage 2                                 CRC-32, MD5, SHA-1, size and name of each file (a sheet's tracks each), relative to
usage 3                                 the library; --comparable in its system's comparable form, a disc as one line
usage 4   rom check [-r] <path>...      each file: ok, or each check it failed (size, sheet, archive, chd)
usage 5   rom dups [<console>]          the groups of the same dump, one a paragraph
usage 6   rom wait [rom<n>]             follow a rom job that went on in the background

case the usage, and what a command line refuses
target none
covers 1-6
$ rom
out 190
Usage: rom hash [-r] [--comparable] <path>... | rom check [-r] <path>... | rom dups [<console>] | rom wait [rom<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library, / for all of it with -r. See man rom.
status 1
action none
$ rom frobnicate
out 190
Usage: rom hash [-r] [--comparable] <path>... | rom check [-r] <path>... | rom dups [<console>] | rom wait [rom<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library, / for all of it with -r. See man rom.
status 1
action none
$ rom hash
out 254
rom hash: name what to hash, or / with -r for the whole library
Usage: rom hash [-r] [--comparable] <path>... | rom check [-r] <path>... | rom dups [<console>] | rom wait [rom<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library, / for all of it with -r. See man rom.
status 1
action none
$ rom check
out 256
rom check: name what to check, or / with -r for the whole library
Usage: rom hash [-r] [--comparable] <path>... | rom check [-r] <path>... | rom dups [<console>] | rom wait [rom<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library, / for all of it with -r. See man rom.
status 1
action none
$ rom check --comparable a.nes
out 238
rom: --comparable is not an option of rom check
Usage: rom hash [-r] [--comparable] <path>... | rom check [-r] <path>... | rom dups [<console>] | rom wait [rom<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library, / for all of it with -r. See man rom.
status 1
action none
$ rom hash -x a.nes
out 227
rom: -x is not an option of rom hash
Usage: rom hash [-r] [--comparable] <path>... | rom check [-r] <path>... | rom dups [<console>] | rom wait [rom<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library, / for all of it with -r. See man rom.
status 1
action none
$ rom dups -r
out 227
rom: -r is not an option of rom dups
Usage: rom hash [-r] [--comparable] <path>... | rom check [-r] <path>... | rom dups [<console>] | rom wait [rom<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library, / for all of it with -r. See man rom.
status 1
action none
$ rom dups snes nes
out 220
rom dups: one console at most
Usage: rom hash [-r] [--comparable] <path>... | rom check [-r] <path>... | rom dups [<console>] | rom wait [rom<n>]
  Paths are relative to the library, / for all of it with -r. See man rom.
status 1
action none
$ rom wait
out 25
rom wait: no such rom job
status 1
action none
$ rom wait rom9
out 30
rom wait: no such rom job rom9
status 1
action none
end
